#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:223
msgid "全エネルギーの収束"
msgstr "Total Energy Convergence"

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:225
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Cu（3.64 Å、スメアリング幅0.02 Ry）とSi（5.47 Å）の全エネルギーが、メッシュを細かくするとどう変わるかを :numref"
":`fig-kp-energy` に示します。\\ 縦軸は、最も細かいメッシュ（Cuは :math:`48^3` 、Siは "
":math:`16^3` ）の値との差の絶対値で、対数軸です。\\ Cuの全エネルギーは、スメアリングを使った計算で最小化される自由エネルギー "
":math:`F` （ :numref:`{number}節 <sec-kp-smearing>` で説明します）です。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-kp-energy` shows how the total energy changes as the mesh "
"gets finer for Cu (3.64 Å, smearing width 0.02 Ry) and Si (5.47 Å). \\ "
"The vertical axis uses a logarithmic scale and gives the absolute "
"difference from the finest-mesh value (:math:`48^3` for Cu and "
":math:`16^3` for Si). \\ For Cu, the total energy plotted here is the "
"free energy :math:`F` that the smearing calculation minimizes (explained "
"in :numref:`Section {number} <sec-kp-smearing>`)."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:233
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"全エネルギーの、最も細かいメッシュの値（参照値）との差 :math:`|E(n)-E(\\mathrm{ref})|` "
"（1原子あたり）。青はCu（3.64 Å、MVスメアリング0.02 Ry、参照は :math:`48^3` ）、オレンジはSi（5.47 "
"Å、固定占有、参照は :math:`16^3` ）。塗りつぶしの点は参照値より高い、白抜きの点は低い値です。点線は1 meV/atom。"
msgstr ""
"Absolute difference in total energy from the finest-mesh value (the "
"reference value), :math:`|E(n)-E(\\mathrm{ref})|`, per atom. Blue shows "
"Cu (3.64 Å, MV smearing at 0.02 Ry, :math:`48^3` reference), and orange "
"shows Si (5.47 Å, fixed occupations, :math:`16^3` reference). Filled "
"points mark values above the reference, and open points mark values below"
" it. The dotted line marks 1 meV/atom."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:235
msgid ""
"Siの差は、 :math:`n` を2増やすごとにおよそ1/5〜1/8になり、片対数のグラフでほぼ直線に並びます。\\ :math:`8^3` "
"で1.9 meV、 :math:`12^3` で0.07 meV/atomです。\\ "
"占有されたバンドのエネルギーはkの滑らかな周期関数なので、等間隔の点での平均（式 :eq:`kp-bz-average` "
"）が、点を増やすと指数関数的に速く正確になるためです。"
msgstr ""
"For Si, each increase of 2 in :math:`n` reduces the difference to about "
"1/5 to 1/8 of its previous value, giving nearly a straight line on the "
"semilog plot. \\ :math:`8^3` gives a difference of 1.9 meV, and "
":math:`12^3` gives 0.07 meV/atom. \\ The energies of the occupied bands "
"are smooth periodic functions of k, so the average over equally spaced "
"points (Equation :eq:`kp-bz-average`) becomes more accurate at an "
"exponential rate as the number of points increases."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:239
msgid ""
"Cuは、 :math:`n` が小さいうちは差が大きく、 :math:`4^3` で155 meV、 :math:`8^3` で31 "
"meV/atomです。\\ :math:`14^3` で1.3 meV、 :math:`16^3` で0.5 "
"meVまで減りますが、そこから先は参照値より低い側に振れ、 :math:`24^3` の差（−0.33 meV）は :math:`20^3` "
"の差（−0.17 meV）より大きくなります。\\ k点を増やせば単調に正確になる、とは限らないのです。\\ 同じ1 "
"meV/atomの精度を得るのに、Siは :math:`10^3` 、Cuは :math:`16^3` "
"が必要で、既約k点の数では47点と145点です。"
msgstr ""
"For Cu, the difference is large at small :math:`n`, reaching 155 meV at "
":math:`4^3` and 31 meV/atom at :math:`8^3`. \\ :math:`14^3` brings the "
"difference down to 1.3 meV and :math:`16^3` to 0.5 meV, but on finer "
"meshes the error changes sign and the energy drops below the reference "
"value. The error at :math:`24^3` (−0.33 meV) is larger in magnitude than "
"at :math:`20^3` (−0.17 meV). \\ Increasing the number of k-points does "
"not necessarily improve accuracy monotonically. \\ To reach the same "
"accuracy of 1 meV/atom, Si needs :math:`10^3` and Cu needs :math:`16^3`, "
"or 47 and 145 irreducible k-points, respectively."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:244
msgid ""
"Quloudの「k グリッド」の既定値は4です。\\ :math:`4\\times4\\times4` では、Cuで155 meV、Siで92 "
"meV/atomのずれがあります。\\ 既定値のまま、全エネルギーの値を議論に使うことはできません。"
msgstr ""
"The default \"k-grid\" value in Quloud is 4. \\ :math:`4\\times4\\times4`"
" gives deviations of 155 meV for Cu and 92 meV/atom for Si. \\ The total "
"energies obtained with the default grid cannot be used to draw "
"conclusions."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:248
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"金属では、 :numref:`{number}節 <sec-kp-mesh>` で見たように、フェルミ面付近の占有数が積分の精度に影響します。\\"
" 今回のCuではスメアリングによって占有数の段差は滑らかになっていますが、フェルミ面付近では依然として急に変化します。\\ "
"メッシュの点とその領域の位置関係が変わるため、誤差は正にも負にもなり、単調には減りません。"
msgstr ""
"In metals, occupation numbers near the Fermi surface affect the accuracy "
"of the integral, as discussed in :numref:`Section {number} <sec-kp-"
"mesh>`. \\ Smearing smooths the step in occupation numbers for Cu, but "
"the occupation numbers still change sharply near the Fermi surface. \\ As"
" the positions of the mesh points relative to that region change, the "
"error can be positive or negative and does not decrease monotonically."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:255
msgid "スメアリング幅"
msgstr "Smearing Width"

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:257
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"金属の計算では、占有数の段差をならすために、占有数を幅 :math:`\\sigma` のなめらかな関数に置き換えます（スメアリング）。\\ "
"このとき自己無撞着に最小化されるのは、全エネルギー :math:`U` から「スメアリングによるエントロピーの項」 :math:`TS` "
"を引いた自由エネルギー :math:`F = U - TS` です。\\ スメアリングの関数の種類と :math:`F` "
"の性質は、技術ノートの\\ `金属のブリルアンゾーン積分 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/metal_bz_integration.html#smearing>`__\\ "
"で説明しています。\\ QEの出力では、 ``!`` で始まる行の ``total energy`` が :math:`F` 、 "
"``smearing contrib. (-TS)`` が :math:`-TS` 、 ``internal energy E=F+TS`` が "
":math:`U` です。\\ :math:`\\sigma \\to 0` で、 :math:`F` も :math:`U` "
"も、スメアリングのない本来の全エネルギーに近づきます（この極限の値は、 :numref:`{number}節 <sec-kp-tetra>` "
"でテトラヘドロン法を使って確かめます）。"
msgstr ""
"In calculations for metals, smearing replaces the step in occupation "
"numbers with a smooth function of width :math:`\\sigma`. \\ The self-"
"consistent calculation minimizes the total energy :math:`U` minus the "
"entropy term :math:`TS` due to smearing, giving the free energy :math:`F "
"= U - TS`. \\ The types of smearing functions and the properties of "
":math:`F` are discussed in \\ `Brillouin zone integration for metals "
"<https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/metal_bz_integration.html#smearing>`__ \\ in the "
"Technical Notes. \\ In the QE output, the line beginning with ``!`` shows"
" ``total energy``, which is :math:`F`. The line labeled ``smearing "
"contrib. (-TS)`` gives :math:`-TS`, and the line labeled ``internal "
"energy E=F+TS`` gives :math:`U`. \\ :math:`\\sigma \\to 0` is the limit "
"in which both :math:`F` and :math:`U` approach the underlying total "
"energy without smearing. We use the tetrahedron method to check this "
"limit in :numref:`Section {number} <sec-kp-tetra>`."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:263
msgid ""
"幅を広げるほど段差がなめらかになり、少ないk点で収束するはずですが、そのかわり :math:`\\sigma \\to 0` "
"の値からずれます。\\ 今回使ったMarzari–Vanderbilt（MV）スメアリング [5]_ は、 :math:`F` の "
":math:`\\sigma` への依存が小さくなるように作られた関数です。\\ Cu（3.64 "
"Å）で幅を0.005、0.01、0.02、0.04 Ryの4通りに変えた結果を :numref:`fig-kp-smearing` に示します。"
msgstr ""
"A wider smearing width smooths the step more, so convergence should "
"require fewer k-points, but the result shifts away from the "
":math:`\\sigma \\to 0` limit. \\ The Marzari–Vanderbilt (MV) smearing "
"[5]_ used here is designed to make :math:`F` weakly dependent on "
":math:`\\sigma`. \\ We tested four smearing widths for Cu (3.64 Å): "
"0.005, 0.01, 0.02, and 0.04 Ry. The results are in :numref:`fig-kp-"
"smearing`."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:271
msgid ""
"Cu（3.64 Å）のMVスメアリングの幅ごとの、自由エネルギー :math:`F` （左）と圧力（右）。左の縦軸は、幅0.005 Ry・ "
":math:`48^3` の :math:`F` との差（1原子あたり）で、4本の曲線に共通の基準です。幅0.04 Ryは "
":math:`40^3` まで計算しました。 :math:`n=8` の点は縦軸の範囲外です。"
msgstr ""
"Free energy :math:`F` (left) and pressure (right) for Cu (3.64 Å) at "
"different MV smearing widths. The vertical axis on the left shows the "
"difference per atom from the value at a width of 0.005 Ry and a "
":math:`48^3` mesh. This value of :math:`F` serves as the reference for "
"all four curves. For 0.04 Ry, we calculated meshes up to :math:`40^3`. "
"The points at :math:`n=8` are outside the vertical axis limits."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:273
msgid "左の図から、2つのことが読み取れます。"
msgstr "The left panel shows two features of convergence."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:275
msgid ""
"**収束の速さ。** 幅が狭いほど、 :math:`n` を増やしたときの振れが大きく、長く続きます。0.005 Ryと0.01 Ryでは "
":math:`24^3` でも基準から1.3〜1.4 meV離れていて、0.005 Ryは :math:`40^3` から "
":math:`48^3` の間でもまだ0.08 meV動いています。0.04 Ryは :math:`20^3` 以降、自分の収束値から0.03 "
"meV以内に収まります。"
msgstr ""
"**Convergence rate.** With smaller widths, fluctuations are larger and "
"persist as :math:`n` increases. At 0.005 Ry and 0.01 Ry, the values are "
"still 1.3 to 1.4 meV from the reference at :math:`24^3`. At 0.005 Ry, the"
" value still changes by 0.08 meV between :math:`40^3` and :math:`48^3`. "
"At 0.04 Ry, the value stays within 0.03 meV of its own converged value "
"from :math:`20^3` onward."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:276
msgid ""
"**収束する値。** 0.005、0.01、0.02 Ryの :math:`F` は、最も細かいメッシュで約0.1 "
"meVの範囲にそろいます。0.04 Ryだけは、それより1.3 meV高い値に収束します。"
msgstr ""
"**Converged values.** At 0.005, 0.01, and 0.02 Ry, the values of "
":math:`F` are within about 0.1 meV of one another on the finest mesh. "
"Only the 0.04 Ry calculation converges to a value 1.3 meV higher."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:278
msgid ""
"圧力（右）でも同じ兼ね合いが見えます。\\ 0.04 Ryの圧力は :math:`16^3` 以降 −12.33〜−12.35 "
"kbarで変わりませんが、狭い3つの幅の最も細かいメッシュでの値（−11.71〜−11.84 kbar）より0.5〜0.6 "
"kbar低くなっています。"
msgstr ""
"Pressure (right) shows the same trade-off. \\ At 0.04 Ry, the pressure "
"stays between −12.33 and −12.35 kbar from :math:`16^3` onward, but it is "
"0.5 to 0.6 kbar lower than the finest-mesh values for the three narrower "
"widths (−11.71 to −11.84 kbar)."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:281
msgid ""
"最も細かいメッシュでの :math:`F` 、 :math:`U` 、 :math:`-TS` を :numref:`tab-kp-"
"smearing` にまとめます。"
msgstr ""
"The values of :math:`F`, :math:`U`, and :math:`-TS` on the finest mesh "
"are listed in :numref:`tab-kp-smearing`."

