":math:`F` と :math:`U` は、幅0.005 Ry・ :math:`48^3` の :math:`F` との差です。\\ "
"幅0.04 Ryでは、 :math:`U` は7.5 meV下がり、 :math:`F` のずれ（1.3 meV）よりずっと大きくずれます。\\ "
"MVスメアリングでは、 :math:`\\sigma \\to 0` の値に近いのは :math:`F` （QEの ``!`` "
"の行）のほうです。\\ なお、MVスメアリングの :math:`-TS` は正にも負にもなり、物理的なエントロピーではありません。"
msgstr ""
":math:`F` and :math:`U` are given as differences from the value at a "
"width of 0.005 Ry and a :math:`48^3` mesh. We use :math:`F` at those "
"settings as the reference for both quantities. \\ At 0.04 Ry, :math:`U` "
"is 7.5 meV below the reference, a much larger deviation than for "
":math:`F` (1.3 meV). \\ With MV smearing, the quantity closer to the "
":math:`\\sigma \\to 0` limit is :math:`F` (the line beginning with ``!`` "
"in the QE output). \\ The term :math:`-TS` in MV smearing can be positive"
" or negative and is not a physical entropy."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:324
msgid ""
"この結果から、今回のCuでは、幅0.02 Ryが兼ね合いのよい選択です。\\ 収束値は狭い幅とほぼ同じ（ :math:`F` で0.1 "
"meV、圧力で0.13 kbar以内）で、狭い幅より振れが小さく、早く収束します。"
msgstr ""
"For Cu in these calculations, a width of 0.02 Ry offers a good balance. "
"\\ The converged values are close to those at narrower widths (within 0.1"
" meV for :math:`F` and 0.13 kbar for pressure), but convergence is faster"
" and the fluctuations are smaller."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:330
msgid "エネルギー差と圧力"
msgstr "Energy Differences and Pressure"

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:332
msgid ""
"格子定数や構造を比べる計算で必要なのは、全エネルギーそのものではなく、格子定数を変えたときのエネルギー差や、圧力です。\\ "
"これらの量は、全エネルギーと同じ速さで収束するのでしょうか。\\ :numref:`fig-kp-differences` "
"に、Cu（スメアリング幅0.02 Ry）の3つの格子定数の結果を示します。\\ ここでは3つの格子定数で共通に計算した最も細かいメッシュ "
":math:`32^3` の値を基準にしました（3.64 Åでは、 :math:`32^3` と :math:`48^3` "
"の差は全エネルギーで0.07 meV、圧力で0.01 kbarです）。"
msgstr ""
"Calculations that compare lattice constants or structures require energy "
"differences as the lattice constant changes, or pressure, rather than the"
" total energy itself. \\ Do those quantities converge as quickly as the "
"total energy? \\ :numref:`fig-kp-differences` shows the results for Cu at"
" three lattice constants with a smearing width of 0.02 Ry. \\ The "
"reference is the finest mesh used for all three lattice constants, "
":math:`32^3`. At 3.64 Å, the :math:`32^3` and :math:`48^3` results differ"
" by 0.07 meV in total energy and 0.01 kbar in pressure."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:341
msgid ""
"Cu（MVスメアリング0.02 Ry）の、 :math:`32^3` の値からのずれ。左：3.64 Åの全エネルギー（灰色）と、格子定数を3.64"
" Åから ±0.04 Å変えたときのエネルギー差（青）。右：3つの格子定数での圧力。縦軸の範囲外の点（ :math:`n` "
"が小さいもの）は描いていません。"
msgstr ""
"Deviations from the :math:`32^3` values for Cu (MV smearing at 0.02 Ry). "
"The left panel shows the total energy at 3.64 Å (gray) and the energy "
"differences when the lattice constant changes by ±0.04 Å from 3.64 Å "
"(blue). The right panel shows pressure deviations at all three lattice "
"constants. Points outside the vertical axis limits (small :math:`n`) are "
"omitted."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:343
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"左の図で、 :math:`12^3` では全エネルギーが5.2 meVずれているのに、エネルギー差のずれは0.1 meV程度です。\\ "
":math:`12^3` から :math:`32^3` まで、 "
":math:`E(3.60\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` は2.93〜3.20 meV、 "
":math:`E(3.68\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` は8.02〜8.23 "
"meVの範囲にあり、ずれは0.16 meV以内です。\\ "
"格子定数が少し違うだけの2つの計算では、同じメッシュによる誤差がほぼ同じだけ入るので、差をとると打ち消し合います。"
msgstr ""
"In the left panel, the :math:`12^3` mesh gives a total energy deviation "
"of 5.2 meV, but the energy differences deviate by only about 0.1 meV. \\ "
":math:`12^3` through :math:`32^3` keep "
":math:`E(3.60\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` between 2.93 and 3.20 meV"
" and :math:`E(3.68\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` between 8.02 and "
"8.23 meV, a deviation of at most 0.16 meV. \\ For two calculations with "
"only slightly different lattice constants, the same mesh introduces "
"nearly the same error in both calculations, so the errors cancel when we "
"take the difference."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:347
msgid ""
"右の図の圧力は、 :math:`12^3` 〜 :math:`20^3` で −0.6〜+0.7 kbarの範囲で振れ、 :math:`24^3`"
" で0.2 kbar以内に収まります。\\ 3つの格子定数で、振れ方がほぼそろっていることにも注目してください。\\ "
"圧力の誤差は、エネルギー差の誤差と同じく、近い格子定数でほぼ共通です。\\ "
"ただし、圧力が0になる格子定数を求めるときは、2つの計算の差をとらないので、この共通の誤差は打ち消されずに残り、求まる格子定数をずらします。\\ "
"3.60 Åと3.68 Åの圧力の差から、圧力の格子定数による変化は約1100 kbar/Åです（ :math:`32^3` ）。\\ "
"圧力の誤差1 kbarは、格子定数の約0.001 Åのずれに相当します。"
msgstr ""
"In the right panel, pressure deviations from :math:`12^3` to :math:`20^3`"
" range between −0.6 and +0.7 kbar and fall within 0.2 kbar at "
":math:`24^3`. \\ Notice that the fluctuations are much the same at all "
"three lattice constants. \\ As with the errors in energy differences, "
"pressure errors are nearly the same at nearby lattice constants. \\ "
"Finding the lattice constant at zero pressure, however, does not involve "
"a difference between two calculations, so this common error does not "
"cancel and shifts the resulting lattice constant. \\ The pressure "
"difference between 3.60 Å and 3.68 Å gives a rate of change in pressure "
"with the lattice constant of about 1100 kbar/Å (at :math:`32^3`). \\ An "
"error of 1 kbar in pressure corresponds to a shift of about 0.001 Å in "
"the lattice constant."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:354
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Siでは、エネルギー差も圧力も速く収束します。\\ :math:`E(5.42\\,\\text{Å})-E(5.47\\,\\text{Å})`"
" は :math:`8^3` で4.277、 :math:`16^3` で4.255 meV/atomで、5.47 Åの圧力は "
":math:`8^3` で −0.38 kbar、 :math:`10^3` 以降は −0.43 kbarで変わりません。"
msgstr ""
"For Si, both energy differences and pressure converge quickly. \\ "
":math:`E(5.42\\,\\text{Å})-E(5.47\\,\\text{Å})` is 4.277 meV/atom at "
":math:`8^3` and 4.255 meV/atom at :math:`16^3`. The pressure at 5.47 Å is"
" −0.38 kbar at :math:`8^3` and stays at −0.43 kbar from :math:`10^3` "
"onward."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:360
msgid "テトラヘドロン法との比較"
msgstr "Comparison with the Tetrahedron Method"

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:362
msgid ""
"ここまでのCuの計算は、すべてスメアリングを使っていました。\\ ここでは、スメアリングを使わない **テトラヘドロン法** "
"で同じ計算を行い、スメアリングと比べます。\\ "
"テトラヘドロン法は、メッシュの点を頂点とする四面体でBZを埋め、その中でバンドのエネルギーを線形に補間して、占有数の段差を含んだまま積分する方法です（技術ノートの\\"
" `金属のブリルアンゾーン積分 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/metal_bz_integration.html#tetrahedron-"
"method>`__）。\\ 線形補間の誤差を補正したBlöchlらの方法 [6]_ と、補間を改良した最適化テトラヘドロン法 [7]_ "
"の2つを使います。\\ QEでは、入力の ``occupations`` を ``'tetrahedra'`` （Blöchlの方法）または "
"``'tetrahedra_opt'`` （最適化テトラヘドロン法）にすると使えます。\\ "
"Quloudの「電子占有数スメアリング」ではテトラヘドロン法を選べないので、入力ファイルを書き換えて計算しました（ "
":doc:`reproduction` ）。"
msgstr ""
"All Cu calculations so far used smearing. \\ Here we repeat the "
"calculations with the **tetrahedron method**, which uses no smearing, and"
" compare the results with smearing. \\ The tetrahedron method fills the "
"BZ with tetrahedra whose vertices are the mesh points. It interpolates "
"the band energies linearly within each tetrahedron to integrate with the "
"discontinuity in the occupation numbers still present (see the Technical "
"Notes page on \\ `Brillouin zone integration for metals <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/metal_bz_integration.html"
"#tetrahedron-method>`__). \\ We use two variants. The method of Blöchl et"
" al. [6]_ corrects the linear interpolation error, and the optimized "
"tetrahedron method [7]_ improves the interpolation itself. \\ In QE, "
"setting ``occupations`` to ``'tetrahedra'`` enables Blöchl's method, and "
"setting it to ``'tetrahedra_opt'`` enables the optimized tetrahedron "
"method. \\ Quloud does not offer the tetrahedron method under "
"\"Electronic occupation number smearing\", so we edited the input file "
"before running the calculations (:doc:`reproduction`)."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:369
msgid ""
"Cuの3つの格子定数で、 :math:`n` = 8〜32（3.64 Åでは48まで）を、2つのテトラヘドロン法で計算しました。\\ "
"占有数のほかは :numref:`tab-kp-conditions` と同じ条件です。\\ 3.64 "
"Åの全エネルギーと圧力を、MVスメアリング0.02 Ryの結果と並べて :numref:`fig-kp-tetra` に示します。"
msgstr ""
"We used both tetrahedron methods at all three Cu lattice constants for "
":math:`n` = 8 to 32 (up to 48 at 3.64 Å). \\ Apart from the occupation "
"numbers, the conditions are the same as in :numref:`tab-kp-conditions`. "
"\\ We compare the total energy and pressure at 3.64 Å with the results "
"for MV smearing at 0.02 Ry in :numref:`fig-kp-tetra`."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:377
msgid ""
"Cu（3.64 Å）の、MVスメアリング0.02 "
"Ry（青、丸）、Blöchlのテトラヘドロン法（緑、四角）、最適化テトラヘドロン法（黄、ひし形）による全エネルギー（左）と圧力（右）。左の縦軸は、最適化テトラヘドロン法の"
" :math:`48^3` の値との差（1原子あたり）で、MVは自由エネルギー :math:`F` です。縦軸の範囲外の点（ :math:`n` "
"が小さいもの）は描いていません。"
msgstr ""
"Total energy (left) and pressure (right) for Cu (3.64 Å) with MV smearing"
" at 0.02 Ry (blue circles), Blöchl's tetrahedron method (green squares), "
"and the optimized tetrahedron method (yellow diamonds). The vertical axis"
" on the left shows the difference per atom from the optimized tetrahedron"
" method at :math:`48^3`. For MV, the energy shown is the free energy "
":math:`F`. Points outside the vertical axis limits (small :math:`n`) are "
"omitted."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:379
msgid ""
"**全エネルギー（左）。** 2つのテトラヘドロン法の値は、 :math:`48^3` で0.003 meV/atomの差で一致しました。\\ "
"スメアリング幅0の極限の値を、スメアリングとは別の方法で求めたことになります。\\ MV 0.02 Ryの :math:`F` は、 "
":math:`48^3` でこれより0.12 meV/atom高い値です。\\ :numref:`tab-kp-smearing` "
"の基準（幅0.005 Ry・ :math:`48^3` の :math:`F` ）は、これより0.17 meV/atom高く、幅0.02 Ryの "
":math:`U` は0.28 meV/atom低い値なので、ここでも幅0の極限に近いのは :math:`F` のほうです。"
msgstr ""
"**Total energy (left).** The two tetrahedron methods gave total energies "
"that differed by 0.003 meV/atom at :math:`48^3`. \\ This gives us the "
"zero-smearing-width limit independently of smearing. \\ For MV at 0.02 "
"Ry, :math:`F` at :math:`48^3` was 0.12 meV/atom above this limit. \\ "
":numref:`tab-kp-smearing` uses a reference (the 0.005 Ry, :math:`48^3` "
"value of :math:`F`) that was 0.17 meV/atom above the limit, while "
":math:`U` at 0.02 Ry was 0.28 meV/atom below it. So here too, :math:`F` "
"is closer to the zero-width limit."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:384
msgid ""
"収束の仕方は、スメアリングとはっきり違います。\\ 最適化テトラヘドロン法は :math:`n` "
"を増やすと上から単調に近づきます。Blöchlの方法は主に下から近づきますが、 :math:`40^3` では自身の :math:`48^3` "
"の値を0.013 meV/atom上回りました。\\ ただし、収束の速さはMVと大きくは変わりません。\\ 自分の :math:`48^3` "
"の値との差が1 meV/atom以内になるのは、MVが :math:`16^3` 、2つのテトラヘドロン法が :math:`20^3` "
"からで、0.1 meV/atom以内になるのはどれも :math:`32^3` からです。"
msgstr ""
"The convergence behavior differs clearly from that of smearing. \\ The "
"optimized tetrahedron method approaches its finest-mesh value "
"monotonically from above as :math:`n` increases. Blöchl's method "
"approaches its finest-mesh value mainly from below, but at :math:`40^3` "
"it was 0.013 meV/atom above its own :math:`48^3` value. \\ However, the "
"convergence rates are similar to that of MV smearing. \\ Each method "
"comes within 1 meV/atom of its own :math:`48^3` value from :math:`16^3` "
"onward for MV and from :math:`20^3` onward for both tetrahedron methods. "
"All three come within 0.1 meV/atom from :math:`32^3` onward."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:389
msgid ""
"**圧力（右）。** 最適化テトラヘドロン法の圧力は、 :math:`14^3` で −11.55 kbar、 :math:`24^3` 以降は "
"−11.68 kbarで変わりません。\\ Blöchlの方法の圧力は、 :math:`8^3` の −12.57 kbarから "
":math:`48^3` の −11.73 kbarまで一方向にゆっくり変わり、 :math:`32^3` でもまだ0.08 "
"kbar動いています。\\ QEは、テトラヘドロン法で力や応力を計算すると、推奨しないという警告（ ``BEWARE: stress "
"calculation with tetrahedra (not recommanded)`` ）を出力します。\\ "
"Blöchlの補正を加えたエネルギーは変分的でないため、そこから求めた応力は、スメアリングの場合ほど信頼できません。\\ "
"最も細かいメッシュでの圧力は、MV 0.02 Ryが −11.71、Blöchlの方法が −11.73、最適化テトラヘドロン法が −11.68 "
"kbarで、0.05 kbarの範囲にそろいました。"
msgstr ""
"**Pressure (right).** The optimized tetrahedron method gives −11.55 kbar "
"at :math:`14^3` and stays at −11.68 kbar from :math:`24^3` onward. \\ "
"With Blöchl's method, the pressure slowly increases from −12.57 kbar at "
":math:`8^3` to −11.73 kbar at :math:`48^3` and is still 0.08 kbar below "
"the finest-mesh value at :math:`32^3`. \\ When forces or stress are "
"calculated with the tetrahedron method, QE issues the warning ``BEWARE: "
"stress calculation with tetrahedra (not recommanded)``. \\ The energy "
"with Blöchl's correction is nonvariational, so stress obtained from it is"
" less reliable than with smearing. \\ On the finest mesh, the pressures "
"were −11.71 kbar for MV at 0.02 Ry, −11.73 kbar for Blöchl's method, and "
"−11.68 kbar for the optimized tetrahedron method, a spread of 0.05 kbar."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:395
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**エネルギー差。** 格子定数を変えたときのエネルギー差は、テトラヘドロン法のほうが粗いメッシュで収束しました。\\ :math:`32^3` "
"の値との差が0.1 meV/atom以内に収まるのは、最適化テトラヘドロン法が :math:`8^3` 、Blöchlの方法が "
":math:`12^3` 、MVが :math:`24^3` からです。\\ :math:`32^3` での値は、 "
":math:`E(3.60\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` が3.03〜3.05 meV/atom、 "
":math:`E(3.68\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` が8.12〜8.14 "
"meV/atomで、3つの方法で0.02 meV以内に一致します。"
msgstr ""
"**Energy differences.** Energy differences between lattice constants "
"converged on coarser meshes with the tetrahedron methods. \\ :math:`32^3`"
" serves as the reference here. The differences stay within 0.1 meV/atom "
"of it from :math:`8^3` onward for the optimized tetrahedron method, from "
":math:`12^3` onward for Blöchl's method, and from :math:`24^3` onward for"
" MV. \\ :math:`32^3` gives 3.03 to 3.05 meV/atom for "
":math:`E(3.60\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})` and 8.12 to 8.14 meV/atom"
" for :math:`E(3.68\\,\\text{Å})-E(3.64\\,\\text{Å})`, so the three "
"methods agree within 0.02 meV."

