#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:427
msgid ""
"全エネルギーは自分の :math:`48^3` の値、エネルギー差と圧力（3.64 Å）は :math:`32^3` "
"の値との差で判定しました。\\ テトラヘドロン法は、同じメッシュでもMVより時間がかかります（ :math:`24^3` で約2〜3倍、 "
":math:`48^3` では4倍以上）。\\ テトラヘドロン法では、既約k点だけでなく、メッシュ全体の四面体（ :math:`6n^3` "
"個）を扱います。\\ SCFの反復全体で占有数の重みの計算にかかった時間（QEの出力の ``sum_band:wei`` ）は "
":math:`24^3` で9〜16秒でした。SCFの最初の反復が始まるまでの時間も、MVの1秒に対して7〜8秒でした。\\ "
":math:`48^3` では、最初の反復が始まるまでに4〜5分かかりました（MVは4秒）。"
msgstr ""
"We assessed total energy against the :math:`48^3` value for each method "
"and energy differences and pressure (3.64 Å) against the :math:`32^3` "
"values. \\ On the same mesh, the tetrahedron methods take longer than MV "
"(about 2 to 3 times as long at :math:`24^3` and more than 4 times as long"
" at :math:`48^3`). \\ The tetrahedron methods handle both the irreducible"
" k-points and the tetrahedra across the entire mesh (:math:`6n^3` of "
"them). \\ Across all SCF iterations, computing the occupation number "
"weights (reported under ``sum_band:wei`` in the QE output) took 9 to 16 "
"seconds in total at :math:`24^3`. Before the first SCF iteration, the "
"tetrahedron methods took 7 to 8 seconds, compared with 1 second for MV. "
"\\ :math:`48^3` required 4 to 5 minutes before the first iteration could "
"start (4 seconds for MV)."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:433
msgid ""
"格子定数を求めるという目的では、最適化テトラヘドロン法は :math:`14^3` （既約k点104点、17秒）で、MV 0.02 Ryの "
":math:`24^3` （413点、18秒）と同じ精度に届きます。\\ "
"計算時間はほぼ同じで、Quloudの画面では選べず、QEも応力の計算には推奨していないので、格子定数の計算にはMVスメアリングを使います。\\ "
"テトラヘドロン法は、スメアリング幅の影響を受けない参照値を得たいときや、状態密度（DOS）の計算に向いています。\\ "
"QuloudのDOS計算でも、SCFのあとのNSCF計算ではテトラヘドロン法が使われます。"
msgstr ""
"For determining the lattice constant, the optimized tetrahedron method at"
" :math:`14^3` (104 irreducible k-points, 17 seconds) reaches the same "
"accuracy as MV at 0.02 Ry with :math:`24^3` (413 points, 18 seconds). \\ "
"We use MV smearing to calculate the lattice constant because the two "
"methods take nearly the same time, the Quloud interface does not offer "
"the optimized tetrahedron method, and QE advises against using it for "
"stress calculations. \\ The tetrahedron method is useful for obtaining "
"reference values unaffected by the smearing width or for calculating the "
"density of states (DOS). \\ For DOS calculations in Quloud, the NSCF "
"calculation after the SCF calculation also uses the tetrahedron method."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:441
msgid "必要なk点メッシュ"
msgstr "Required k-Point Mesh"

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:443
msgid ""
"ここまでの結果を、量ごとに「どのメッシュから許容誤差に収まるか」でまとめます（ :numref:`tab-kp-summary` ）。\\ 表の "
":math:`n` は、そのメッシュと、それより細かい計算したすべてのメッシュで、参照値との差が許容誤差以内になる最小の :math:`n` "
"です。\\ 参照値は、Cuの全エネルギーは :math:`48^3` 、Cuのエネルギー差と圧力は :math:`32^3` 、Siはすべて "
":math:`16^3` の値です。"
msgstr ""
"For each quantity, we summarize how fine the mesh needs to be to meet "
"each tolerance (:numref:`tab-kp-summary`). \\ Each :math:`n` in the table"
" is the smallest :math:`n` for which that mesh and every finer mesh we "
"tested give values within the stated tolerance of the reference value. \\"
" The reference values come from :math:`48^3` for Cu total energy, "
":math:`32^3` for Cu energy differences and pressure, and :math:`16^3` for"
" all Si quantities."

#: ../../kpoints/kpoint_convergence.rst:447
msgid "許容誤差に収まるk点メッシュ :math:`n`"
msgstr "k-point meshes :math:`n` meeting each tolerance"

